{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1261025-let-s-make-a-flower-of-despair-bloom-spring-razor-green-jade-artifact-4-daiklave","id":1261025,"title":"Let's make a flower of despair bloom (Spring Razor Green Jade Artifact 4 Daiklave)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-16T16:58:13-07:00","id":1261025,"title":"Let's make a flower of despair bloom (Spring Razor Green Jade Artifact 4 Daiklave)","content":"I needed a warmup before starting the Alchemical Combat charm remake anywho.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Spring Razor (Artifact 4 Green Jade Daiklave)</span></b><br /> <br /> This a remake of Spring Razor in order to match current Arms of the Chosen standards. We all know the fluff of it already, so let\u2019s just dive into it shall we?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sidebar: Can I make this into a bow instead?</b></span><br /> The bow version of this artifact is called the Green Death. It functionally has the same charms. At least until some other artifact comes out.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement</b>: 5m<br /> <b>Type</b>: Medium (+3 ACC, +12L DMG, +1 DEF, OVW 5)<br /> <b>Tags</b>: Lethal, Melee, Balanced<br /> <b>Hearthstone slot(s)</b>: 1, in the pommel<br /> <b>Era</b>: Sometime during the Shogunate<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement</b>: Any character resonant to Jade/Green Jade may learn the charm Howling Lotus Strike for free. Exigents relating to the purview of plants, wood, or flowers may also treat themselves as resonant with this artifact, though some such as the Chosen of Sunflowers use parasols instead.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>HOWLING LOTUS STRIKE</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1; <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only, Resonant<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: None<br /> <br /> The Spring Razor\u2019s tip glows green with poisonous essence where even the slightest nick dooms an opponent to their fate. The opponent immediately makes a check for poison that has the traits of Arrow Frog Venom (Page 234 Exalted Core). If using the rules for Strong-type opponents, you may apply this charm on a <b>withering </b>attack against Strong type opponents.<br /> <br /> This evocation can be used without damaging the opponent for free to anyone stupid enough to lick Spring Razor. It is not advised to make this your sword-wife. Throwing it into a Tyrant Lizard\u2019s mouth will cause it to suffer the effects of Howling Lotus Strike until it perishes.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant</b>: Instead of Arrow Frog Venom the wielder may transfer any poison she currently suffers from into the Spring Razor and subsequently into the opponent. The poison shares all the same stats as it normally does, but only the duration is whatever the wielder had left on it instead. This feature comes with a +1m surcharge.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>VENOM INTENSIFYING STROKE</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1; <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Stackable, Uniform<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Howling Lotus Strike<br /> <br /> The Spring Razor glows a bright green with ethereal rose petals following in the blade\u2019s wake. This charm increases the damage and duration of a single poison the target is suffering from by 1. This charm stacks, so being attacked twice increases the duration of the poison by 2 turns and damage by 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Dissonant</b>: This charm may only be stacked up to (2 or Essence, higher) additional turns.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>SEVEN WIDOWS VENOM</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: -; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2; <b>Type</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Venom Intensifying Stroke<br /> <br /> The bite of a twice scorned lover is more lethal than any known animal. This charm alters the poison from Howling Lotus Strike. Its duration cannot be lowered below a single turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Conditions</b>: This charm may be learned for free if the wielder has Appearance 4+ or a speciality in some sort of elegant fighting style for Melee. This charm cannot be learned at all by Hideous characters.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>FORCING OPEN THE EYE OF BEAUTY</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: - (1WP); <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3; <b>Type</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Seven Widows Venom<br /> <br /> To the philistines who do not have an eye for the finer arts in life, one has to show them the way. This charm enhances Howling Lotus Strike. By paying a 1WP surcharge the wielder may even poison things that are immune to poison, such as Automatons and the Undead. Additionally if a creature is immune to Spring Razor\u2019s venom, she may activate this charm to immediately create a new venom on the spot from the innumerable plant based poisons in nature, causing the opponent the need to resist it all over.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant</b>: This charm can only be learned by wielders Resonant with this weapon and Appearance 4+.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>DEADLY FLOWERS BLOOMING</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1m 1i; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2; <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Stackable, Uniform<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Venom Intensifying Stroke<br /> <br /> The Spring Razor draws upon its enemy\u2019s own life force to further power and amplify the poisons that exist within so they blossom to full bloom. This charm may only be used once per turn on the wielder\u2019s turn, causing any successful attack (IE: Doing damage) to grow pink lotus flowers on Spring Razor and committing the cost of this charm. Once three activations have been stacked the flowers blossom into full bloom. At this point any attempt to knock the blade out of the wielders hand (including but not limited to disarm actions or Larceny charms) only knock the flowers off the blade rather than the Spring Razor out of the wielder\u2019s hand. Additionally the duration and damage of all poisons inflicted by the Spring Razor are increased by 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Dissonant</b>: The cost of this charm is 2m 2i.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>DELICATE CRIMSON EXECUTION</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m 1WP <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3; <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Deadly Flowers Blooming, Seven Widows Venom<br /> <br /> This charm works the same as on Page 621 of the Exalted 3e Corebook.<br /> <br /> Veins of pink-and-crimson Essence flash across Spring Razor\u2019s edge as it makes a fateful cut, granting its target the gifts of beauty and death. After being successfully struck with this attack, flowers begin to slowly appear and blossom across the target\u2019s body. On each of the target\u2019s subsequent turns, these flowers lessen the duration of all poisons afflicting the target by 1, and grow closer to achieving full bloom. After consuming four intervals of poison, the flowers unfurl and flood the victim\u2019s system with concentrated, Essence-enriched toxins, immediately inflicting poison damage equal to twice the damage they prevented by consuming intervals of active poisons. If the victim has no poison intervals in his system for the flowers to consume, their growth stalls. In either case, they sublimate into Essence at the end of the scene. This Evocation can\u2019t be directed against the same target twice in a scene.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>SWIRLING PETAL DEFENSE</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1; <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Uniform<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: None<br /> <br /> Both the body and blade of the wielder move with shimmering lotus petals, sowing confusion and disorientation in their wake. This charm may be used after a successful defense, releasing a spray of petals in the direction of the attacker up to close range away. If the defense is successful the assailant takes a -3 penalty to all non-reflexive dice pools and a -1 to their defense until the end of the wielder\u2019s next turn.<br /> <br /> If the wielder knows Essence Blossom Escape at Essence 2+ she may repurchase this charm, causing a -4 to all dicepools and a -2 penalty to the afflicted defense. This feature is gained for free if the wielder has 4 or more appearance.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant</b>: The wielder may apply the penalty to any Stamina+Resistance checks against poison.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>ESSENCE BLOSSOM ESCAPE</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4m 1WP; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1; <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Swirling Pedal Defense<br /> <br /> The wielder of the Spring Razor makes a quick leap behind her, leaving a sudden burst of lotus petals to daze and confuse those left behind. This charm may be used to supplement a disengage attempt by applying a -2 penalty to anyone contesting her. If the wielder is successful then everyone who failed is immediately subjected to Swirling Petal Defense\u2019s penalties and the wielder regains one willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Dissonant</b>: Dissonant wielders do not gain this point of willpower.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">WHIRLING PETAL STORM</span></b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 6m 1WP; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3; <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Resonant<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Until the end of next turn<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Essence Blossom Escape<br /> <br /> Spring Razor glows a bright pink before being swung through the air, coating the battlefield with shimmering rose petals.The wielder makes a melee attack roll against every target within short range. If successful the attack does no damage but rather everyone inside of it suffers the effects of Swirling Petal Defense\u2019s penalties. If this attack afflicts two or more targets successfully then the user regains a single point of willpower.<br /> <br /> If the wielder has Appearance 4+ then she adds a single automatic success on the attack roll and extends the range of this charm to medium. She needs to successful attack 3 people in order to gain the benefits of this charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Dissonant</b>: Wielders do not regain the willpower used in this charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant</b>: The shimmering Lotus petals of essence are difficult to see through, causing anyone outside the radius of the petal storm to have a -3 penalty to any and all ranged attacks which does not stack with Swirling Petal Defense\u2019s penalties. If this weapon is a bow then the wielder takes no penalties for shooting into the storm.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>THE FLOWERING OF CREATION</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: -; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3; <b>Type</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Resonant<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Delicate Crimson Execution, Whirling Petal Storm<br /> <br /> Dying by Spring Razor may not be one of the most painful deaths one may suffer, but it is amongst the most graceful. This charm may be activated whenever an opponent suffering from Delicate Crimson Execution dies, either by the poison or by any other normal death. After a few parting words the victim explodes into a cloud of lotus petals, allowing the Exalt to activate Whirling Petal Storm reflexively. Additionally anyone affected are treated as being immediately hit by Howling Lotus Strike.<br /> <br /> If the wielder knows Bedecked in Death and Beauty they may repurchase this charm at Essence 5. For a +4m 3i surcharge she may cause the ground below her to rapidly flower and bloom pink lotus petals out to medium range. This causes everyone inside this area minus the wielder to suffer the effects of Howling Lotus Strike every turn. If multiple people die as a result of Bedecked in Death and Beauty then the damage and the duration of the poison increases by 1 per dead body in the overlapping area (Battle groups instead use size).<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant</b>: This charm is a very graceful way to die, causing all beholders to swear off death because of the noble end the Spring Razor\u2019s wielder bequeathed to them. Upon activating this feature the wielder may instead elect to make a special Appearance + Presence roll against the Resolve of everyone present. People cannot elect to use the victim who perished as an intimacy to raise their Resolve, but any other intimacy is fine. If successful those afflicted are compelled not to take revenge against the wielder of the Spring Razor, instead seeing the death of the victim as one of the best possible ways one could leave this world. Pink Lotus petals will grow on the spot where the victim died and on top of his grave.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>BEDECKED IN DEATH AND BEAUTY</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m 2i 1WP; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 4; <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Delicate Crimson Execution, Whirlwind Petal Storm<br /> <br /> The spray of essence petals collect on a victim's skin, quickly forming flowers that lead to their demise. This charm may only be used whenever two or more people are placed under the affliction of Swirling Petal Defense\u2019s penalty effect, generated either by it or charms that use it. Everyone affected by it immediately begins suffering the effects of Delicate Crimson Execution.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T05:17:22-07:00","id":1261088,"title":"","content":"Nice to see some of the alpha version of the artifact coming back. Petal Storm!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T06:00:37-07:00","id":1261096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/